 credNote:"As credited on the 2001 reissue plus musicians identified by later research; individual track line-ups were never fully documented.",
 text:[
 "After years of having his songs passed over within the Beatles, Harrison emptied his stockpile in one go: two LPs of songs and a third disc of studio jams, co-produced with Phil Spector's towering “Wall of Sound”. Often called rock's first triple album, it was made with a who's-who of friends – the core of the band became Derek and the Dominos – in sessions Harrison ran with incense, an altar and none of the pressure of his old group.",
 "<strong>Then:</strong> near-universal acclaim. <em>Rolling Stone</em>'s Ben Gerson called it “the <em>War and Peace</em> of rock 'n' roll”, and <em>Melody Maker</em>'s Richard Williams wrote “Garbo talks! – Harrison is free!” It topped the charts in the UK, the US and Norway, among many others, and “My Sweet Lord” was a worldwide No. 1.",
 "<strong>Now:</strong> widely considered the finest solo Beatle album. Mikal Gilmore (<em>Rolling Stone</em>) called it “the finest solo work any ex-Beatle ever produced”; the 2021 50th-anniversary remix returned it to No. 1 in the Scottish chart and the US rock albums chart."],
 beatles:[{kind:"quote",who:"John Lennon, 1970",text:"“I think it's all right, you know. Personally, at home, I wouldn't play that kind of music… I don't want to hurt George's feelings… I think it's better than Paul's.”",src:"https://www.rollingstone.com/music/music-news/lennon-remembers-part-one-186693/",srcName:"Rolling Stone, “Lennon Remembers”"},
  {kind:"quote",who:"John Lennon, 1980",text:"“I think <em>All Things Must Pass</em> was all right. It just went on too long.” On the “My Sweet Lord” plagiarism case: “He could have changed a couple of bars in that song and nobody could ever have touched him…”",src:"http://www.beatlesinterviews.org/db1980.jlpb.beatles.html",srcName:"Playboy interview, 1980"},
  {kind:"fact",who:"Ringo Starr",text:"Ringo was one of the album's main drummers and also helped Harrison cut the pre-session demos with Klaus Voormann."}],
