 text:[
 "It began as a B-side. Harrison needed an extra song for a European single, and the friends he gathered at Bob Dylan's garage studio wrote “Handle with Care” in an afternoon. The song was too good to waste, so the five became a band of made-up half-brothers, the Traveling Wilburys, and recorded the album in spring 1988.",
 "<strong>Then:</strong> a hit with critics and buyers alike. It went triple platinum in the US, won the Grammy for Best Rock Performance by a Duo or Group, and was nominated for Album of the Year. Critics loved how relaxed and modest it was.",
 "<strong>Now:</strong> still loved, and <em>Mojo</em> and <em>Uncut</em> give it full marks. Roy Orbison died in December 1988, just weeks after its release."],
